{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual","id":1069595,"title":"Verbena ritual","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-28T13:50:01-07:00","id":1069595,"title":"Verbena ritual","content":"Alright, I finnaly decided to play a Verbena character. <br /> So, I thought about one ritual (I made it).<br /> The question is: is it possible and what spheres would it require?<br /> <br /> Basically, you are channeling a vampire. You constantly use him to lower your difficulty for Arete rolls (like spending quintessence) only thing is that you spend HIS vitae... I thought about like making 2 vampire's blood points = 1 quintessence point... Verbena mages magick is litteraly consuming vampire's magic.<br /> Is it possible, what spheres I need and at what rank ? I thought about Prime and Correspondence...<br /> What rules would you apply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:41:20-07:00","id":1069629,"title":"","content":"First of all, what kind of backstory does this Verbena have that means they have a vampire who would be ok with this? Most vampire's I'm aware of would probably have something to say about being reduced to some dirt mage's personal periapt.<br /> <br /> Now, spheres, you'll definitely need Prime 2 at least to absorb quintessence from the Tass which is the vampire's blood. Prime 3 would probably be better if the blood is inside the vampire and the vampire is willing, and Prime 4 if the vampire is not willing.<br /> <br /> You may need a combination of Life and Matter spheres in order to target their blood pool, Matter 1 Life 1 should be enough, though arguably you might need Life 2 and Matter 2 in order to decouple the quintessence from the vampire's blood (since it's no ordinary tass). But that depends on what your ST rules.<br /> <br /> Correspondence is required equal to the highest ranked sphere in order to do any of this at a distance, so if you need Prime 4, you'll also need Corr. 4 to match it.<br /> <br /> Depending on how your ST rules it, you'd have to get a lot of successes in order to combat things like countermagic (which all Splats seem to get in most crossover rules), and you may be limited by your avatar regarding how much you can absorb into your magic in a single sitting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, prepare to put a big shiny &quot;drain here&quot; target on your neck for trying this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:47:38-07:00","id":1069636,"title":"","content":"I thought about locking him somewhere... <br /> So Prime 4,Corresponde 4, Life and Matter 1?<br /> <br /> What about taking his blood.. That would be a Tass, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:24:56-07:00","id":1069732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual?p=1069636#post1069636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought about locking him somewhere...<br /> So Prime 4,Corresponde 4, Life and Matter 1?<br /> <br /> What about taking his blood.. That would be a Tass, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be yes.<br /> <br /> It would also be suicide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:29:21-07:00","id":1069733,"title":"","content":"I really hope book of secrets includes or updates the ghouled mage rules from blood treachery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:32:38-07:00","id":1069734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual?p=1069732#post1069732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be yes.<br /> <br /> It would also be suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. Do you really think they track down what happens to every missing vampire? I mean. They could just get blindsided by a truck one night and not manage to pull themselves up until after the sun comes up and bam. you're hunting a pile of ashes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T22:01:37-07:00","id":1069867,"title":"","content":"I think just taking the quintessence from the already extracted vampire blood with Prime 2 would be the simplest way of going about it. If you don't want to have to carry the blood around, you can store it somewhere very familiar to you and use Correspondence 2 and Prime 2 to access it. Happy hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-29-2017, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T22:13:40-07:00","id":1069871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual?p=1069867#post1069867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think just taking the quintessence from the already extracted vampire blood with Prime 2 would be the simplest way of going about it. If you don't want to have to carry the blood around, you can store it somewhere very familiar to you and use Correspondence 2 and Prime 2 to access it. Happy hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enjoy that resonance though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T22:23:51-07:00","id":1069879,"title":"","content":"Roasted Spicy Chana Jhor!<br /> <br /> It's to die for!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-29-2017, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T22:58:16-07:00","id":1069897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual?p=1069733#post1069733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope book of secrets includes or updates the ghouled mage rules from blood treachery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they don't. I never liked Blood Treachery's rules. They felt draconian, and reinforced an interpretation of why Embraced mages lose their Avatars that I believe reduces the number of stories that could be told. (If the Avatar simply moves on, rather than being destroyed, it serves the same purpose, while also creating the situation where two incarnations of the same soul are running around simultaneously).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:03:27-07:00","id":1069947,"title":"","content":"I'm going to point out that the Verbena are one of the more anti-Vampire Traditions when it comes to the average (Life-focused, wiccan/old gods/new age) member, so a Verbena 'tainting' themself by using the vampire's power to fuel their own requires...a rather unusual Verbena character with an equally unusual Verbena paradigm where this is acceptable or par for the course.<br /> <br /> It's a very Hermetic thing to do, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-29-2017, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T05:02:30-07:00","id":1069980,"title":"","content":"The easiest way is indeed to treat it as some kind of lame tass. Pick a less favorable conversion ratio (2:1 or 3:1) and go have fun with prime 2 for the collected blood, or extracting it via prime 5 or life 3 matter 3.<br /> <br /> The main complications are:<br /> while stealing back the vitae is nice, it's not all fun and games... it's an energy already tainted to the verbena eye in so many ways. I'd totally include some purification process before that is available.<br /> <br /> unwilling targets are a crapshoot. Also automatic fuck you resonance, so not worth it :|","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T05:05:55-07:00","id":1069985,"title":"","content":"Don't worry about the resonance. All you have to do is ensure that you consume tass of varied resonances... Let's try a similar thing for Spirits, Werewolves, Demons, Mummies, and Changeling now! (says the bad idea bear)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T05:26:14-07:00","id":1069989,"title":"","content":"You're thinking of resonance as in your signature and the effects on you. I am talking about the resonance of the tass itself and how it, well, resonates with what you want to do.<br /> <br /> Like how a resonance of empathy and simpathy is good for healing or sensing emotions.<br /> A resonance of fuck you will literally always count as inappropriate for whatever you want to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T05:42:58-07:00","id":1069996,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously, you'll want to use your quintessence to cast magick to catch more creatures to suck tass from <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think Vampire resonance will be particularly suited for that<br /> Gotta catch them all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T06:16:30-07:00","id":1070010,"title":"","content":"Quintessence extracted from an unwilling creature pretty much always comes with this bad resonance. It's part of why you don't really do that unless you're that desperate or do it for the kicks. It happily coincides with how these kind of people always do some absurdly elaborate rituals...gotta bring forth other resonances to compensate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T07:26:05-07:00","id":1070047,"title":"","content":"Actually, according to Mage Revised, it's not just bad resonance. Unwilling victims usually generate an equal and opposite measure of psychic Resonance absolutely opposed to the murderer and everything he or she stands for and that even willingly given quintessence is usually inefficient and loaded with Resonance. Of course, the former refers to the example of a murder of a victim in a nephandic ritual.<br /> <br /> My guess is that, since the vampires took the blood from possibly unwilling victims themselves and the vampire isn't actually being murdered, this mitigates some of that opposing resonance and brings it from &quot;impossible to collect quintessence from&quot; to &quot;usually inefficient and loaded with Resonance&quot;. Vampire blood is considered tass after all so there must be a certain set of effects it can be used for, otherwise there would be no point in calling it tass. Maybe sucking the magic out of other things would be appropriately themed.<br /> <br /> IN M20, anything related to resonance seems to have become an optional rule and vampire blood is still considered tass.<br /> <br /> That said, going around treating creatures as your personal quintessence batteries is just asking for trouble... but I still want to see someone do it in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T07:36:38-07:00","id":1070054,"title":"","content":"I don't think that second connection's really convincing :/<br /> <br /> For one unless you're explicitly returning it to the owner somehow it's easy to say nothing's changed.<br /> For another that takes away the power of the Curse of the vampires, makes their Atrocities less the nature of the monster and more just the actions of a cannibal sociopath. Vampires are more than that.<br /> <br /> We all agree it's tass. I'm just saying stealing it from the vampire will come loaded with heaps of bad stuff, even if it's &quot;stealing from thieves&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW Just double checked. Resonance is kind of three things. It appears as a modifier to spellcasting, and in the &quot;optional rule&quot; boards as the imprints of things and (synergy) how they manifest.<br /> Nothing is explicited about the first element, and is the one i'm referring to here.<br /> <br /> I'm treating it as mandatory here, but if you don't want to use them just be aware that much of the &quot;cooties&quot; from the OP's workings will go away. You'll be left only with the direct conversion and non-magickal implications of stealing someone's blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 03-29-2017, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:28:17-07:00","id":1070099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual?p=1070054#post1070054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one unless you're explicitly returning it to the owner somehow it's easy to say nothing's changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if nothing has changes, that would mean it's completely unusable, according to revised (unless the vampire fed from willing victims). My assessment of what the difference is might be wrong but something has to be different here or vampire blood would not be useable tass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual?p=1070054#post1070054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For another that takes away the power of the Curse of the vampires, makes their Atrocities less the nature of the monster and more just the actions of a cannibal sociopath. Vampires are more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not contesting this point so much as asking how this is so. I don't understand your logic here at this point<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual?p=1070054#post1070054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm treating it as mandatory here, but if you don't want to use them just be aware that much of the &quot;cooties&quot; from the OP's workings will go away. You'll be left only with the direct conversion and non-magickal implications of stealing someone's blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, I was looking for it in M20 and couldn't find anything on it. If I'm to incorporate something like that in my games I'd prefer some hard rules on it rather than notations in the rotes of a previous edition. That said, I'm not the OP's storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:49:21-07:00","id":1070116,"title":"","content":"I'm just questioning your logic on how vitae tass is less bad because you're taking it from the vampire. At this point it's already the vampire's blood... and yeah it's a mess.<br /> <br /> On the rules: The <b>trait</b> resonance is treated as optional and explained there in pages 560 and 561, there the trait is detailed. Meanwhile in page 503, the chart for magickal difficulties, resonance appears without any other explanation. Just &quot;appropriate/inappropriate&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T09:12:16-07:00","id":1070137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual?p=1070116#post1070116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just questioning your logic on how vitae tass is less bad because you're taking it from the vampire. At this point it's already the vampire's blood... and yeah it's a mess.<br /> <br /> On the rules: The <b>trait</b> resonance is treated as optional and explained there in pages 560 and 561, there the trait is detailed. Meanwhile in page 503, the chart for magickal difficulties, resonance appears without any other explanation. Just &quot;appropriate/inappropriate&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my logic could be wrong, but just to clear up what I was saying:<br /> Vampire Blood is Tass. If blood taken from an unwilling vampire and used for quintessence has the same problems as the quintessence taken from a sacrificed mortal, then the blood taken from a vampire would be utterly useless (as noted in mage revised). Therefore, something must be different with taking vampire blood and spilling the blood of an unwilling mortal. I suggested in a badly worded way that since you are not the victim's murderer and the blood belonged to the victim rather than the vampire, the resonance is not innately opposed to your very being and is perhaps more opposed to the vampire. Even if you kill the vampire, I thought maybe they wouldn't be able to taint it in the same way as the original owner or their being or killed hurt is not opposed by the resonance of the blood taken from their victims (because otherwise it would provide no quintessence). Therefore, while loaded with bad resonance, the vampire blood is still useable for certain types of magick, rather than utterly useless.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-29-2017, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T13:45:07-07:00","id":1070277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1069595-verbena-ritual?p=1070137#post1070137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, my logic could be wrong, but just to clear up what I was saying:<br /> Vampire Blood is Tass. If blood taken from an unwilling vampire and used for quintessence has the same problems as the quintessence taken from a sacrificed mortal, then the blood taken from a vampire would be utterly useless (as noted in mage revised). Therefore, something must be different with taking vampire blood and spilling the blood of an unwilling mortal. I suggested in a badly worded way that since you are not the victim's murderer and the blood belonged to the victim rather than the vampire, the resonance is not innately opposed to your very being and is perhaps more opposed to the vampire. Even if you kill the vampire, I thought maybe they wouldn't be able to taint it in the same way as the original owner or their being or killed hurt is not opposed by the resonance of the blood taken from their victims (because otherwise it would provide no quintessence). Therefore, while loaded with bad resonance, the vampire blood is still useable for certain types of magick, rather than utterly useless.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The difference here, is the sacrificial mortal doesn't CONTAIN tass. They are, like every other thing, MADE OF tass. When you sacrifice a mortal for quintessence, what you're doing is unmaking them and trying to redirect some of the quintessence that spills from their form into your cup, rather than just back into the tapestry. You can do the same thing with physical objects and things as well.<br /> <br /> Since that quintessence is THEM, they say &quot;No, you go fuck yourself&quot; and defy gravity to make sure none of their life-juice goes into your cup.<br /> <br /> A vampires Vitae on the other hand. Is not their constructive tass. If you take it away they suffer ill effects, of course, but you don't have to literally unmake them to get at it. So using it is MUCH MUCH EASIER. Though not without it's difficulties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T14:19:07-07:00","id":1070294,"title":"","content":"What about werewolf claws?<br /> <br /> Edit: That does make more sense, what you wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-29-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}